"Purpose & Standards\r\n🎯 Purpose & Standards\r\n🪖 Mission\r\nDeliver a prompt, personal, value-driven quoting experience from first contact through onboarding, turning qualified opportunities into well-documented clients.\r\n➕ Standards of Success\r\n* Respond Quickly. Respond within 5 minutes, enter quotes within 2 hours, and deliver standard quotes within 24 hours; complex quotes may take up to 4 days.\r\n* Quote Completely. Enter data digitally, use EZLynx/Tarmika, track every viable market, and save each generated quote in the correct Quotes or Submission Center tab.\r\n* Present Value. Present quotes directly before emailing them, apply agency coverage standards, and complete all required documentation.\r\n🗂️ EZLynx & File Standards\r\n* Discussion title — New Business\r\n* Automation Center — Sales Center\r\n* Folder — New Business/Application/Declarations; for each commercial submission, create a separate Submission Center folder for that submission\r\n* Document labels — Policy \r\n* EZLynx labels — New Business Follow Up; New Business Follow Up Spanish\r\n🚫 Non-Negotiables (Unacceptable Actions)\r\n* Never Skip Presentation. Do not email a quote before presenting it directly or omit required coverage review and documentation.\r\n* Follow Payment Rules. Use EFT monthly or annual when possible; use other payment options only when the premium exceeds $1,000.\r\n* Apply Required Fees. Charge the $100 agency fee on manual policies except one-day events, and add a supporting line when applicable.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStandard Operating Procedures\r\n📋 Standard Operating Procedure\r\nStep 1 — New\r\nRole: CSR for intake; Producer for qualification\r\n* Capture the lead’s name, phone, correct lead source, line of business, and X-date in EZLynx. Do not request a declarations page at intake.\r\n* Warm-transfer to an available Producer. If unavailable, the CSR gathers basic information, schedules a Calendly appointment, assigns the EZLynx task, and marks it with “!”.\r\n* The Producer builds rapport, confirms why the prospect is shopping, identifies every policy opportunity, sets decision expectations, and next steps\r\n* If you speak to the client  we must move the client to “Contacted” in the Salescenter pipeline to avoid automation follow up (only if we speak to the client if not then let the automation follow up). \r\nStep 2 — Contacted\r\nRole: Producer\r\n* Move the opportunity to Contacted. Apply department coverage standards and gather underwriting data through approved research sources, PURL links, carrier databases, and the correct line-of-business questions.\r\n* Enter the application directly into EZLynx/Tarmika, the carrier site, or Wunderrite/Submission Center. Upload every quote to the correct Quotes or Submission Center tab.\r\n* For off-phone quoting, book the presentation appointment, create the EZLynx task, follow up diligently, and never email the quote before presenting it.\r\nStep 3 — Quoted\r\nRole: Producer\r\n* Firm up rates, reports, exclusions, subjectivities, and coverage-standard compliance. Quote every applicable carrier and prepare two or three coverage options.\r\n* Call the prospect to present the quote. Explain the selected carrier, at least three benefits, coverage differences, discounts, exclusions, and monthly premium differences.\r\n* Confirm decision timing and book follow-up before presenting. Ask for the business: selected option, signature email, and payment method.\r\n* Use the approved CENT framework for objections. If the prospect does not bind, schedule the next appointment and move to Reviewed.\r\nStep 4 — Review & Close\r\nRole: Producer\r\n* Create and share the EZLynx Submission Center proposal; use Personal Quotes Proposal Beta for personal proposals.\r\n* Move the opportunity to Reviewed and tell the customer to expect the Client Center email/text.\r\n* Follow the approved New Business follow-up process for up to 14 days unless the prospect directs otherwise. Keep a specific next-contact time.\r\n* Close the outcome correctly: qualified rejection to X-date, unqualified rejection to Dead, more time to a two-day follow-up cadence for two weeks, or accepted business to Won.\r\nStep 5- WON!\r\nRole: Producer\r\n* Thank the client, move the opportunity to Won, and record the finalized carrier and premium in Sales Center.\r\n* Upload all applications, checklists, signed documents, correspondence, and required subjectivities.\r\n* Explain next steps, carrier onboarding requirements, discounts, Client Center, and the incoming welcome email/text; then proceed to Binding.\r\n* Return newly bound or recently rewritten underwriting issues to the originating Producer. The Producer speaks with the insured before reassignment; renewals go to the department renewal team.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat Ifs\r\n🙃 What Ifs\r\nPolicy Not Bound or Active\r\nTell the client clearly by phone and in writing that coverage is not yet bound or active and that the team is completing the required steps.\r\n\r\nCarrier Website Is Unavailable\r\nAlert the team lead.\r\n\r\nPayment Missing or Declined\r\nDo not proceed as though coverage is active; alert the team lead.\r\n\r\n\r\nCarrier Documents Not Signed\r\nAlert the Producer who wrote the policy.\r\n\r\n\r\nDiscount Information Missing\r\nAlert the Producer who wrote the policy and obtain the missing insured information.\r\n\r\n\r\nInspection or Underwriting Memo Generated\r\nAlert the Producer who wrote the policy.\r\n\r\n\r\nNo Binding Documentation After Two Follow-Ups\r\nAfter two follow-up attempts, alert the Producer who wrote the policy.\r\n\r\n\r\nReceived Policy Does Not Match Request\r\nAlert the team lead before proceeding.\r\n\r\n\r\nMore Opportunities Needed\r\nComplete 15 active cold calls or drop-ins monthly, 45 quarterly, and 180 annually.\r\n\r\n\r\nReferral and Cross-Sell\r\nBuild referral relationships; call sold clients twice monthly for referrals; cross-sell monoline clients; work lost customers and unsold quotes.\r\n\r\n\r\nClosing Unsold Quotes\r\nClose unsold quotes only after at least eight follow-up attempts within two weeks.\r\n\r\n\r\nProspect Resists Rapport Building\r\nConfirm the prospect fits the agency, adjust tone, and use appropriate humor to build connection.\r\n\r\n\r\nProspect Focuses Only on Price\r\nLead with education, clarify desired protection, show value, emphasize speed and convenience, and be willing to walk away when the fit is wrong.\r\n\r\n\r\nProspect Is Not a Good Fit or Goes MIA\r\nUse the approved decline or break-up process, complete follow-up, and set a six-month contact activity if there is no reply.\r\n\r\n\r\nLow Closing Ratio\r\nReview whether New Business steps are being skipped. Every prospect must be placed into and managed through the full process.\r\n\r\n\r\nInsured Has Class 2 Pickups\r\nCoverwhale may cover vehicles from 6,001 through 10,000 pounds; use the Hotshot Guidelines resource.\r\n\r\n\r\nCustomer Does Not Reply\r\nUse postal mail when appropriate to the severity and apply the New Business Follow Up label.\r\n\r\n\r\nContact Information Is Wrong\r\nUse postal mail and send the Bad Contact memo.\r\n\r\n\r\nCustomer Is Hospitalized or Uses a Caretaker\r\nAdd the caretaker as an EZLynx contact, schedule a meeting when the customer is available, and complete the standard follow-up process.\r\n\r\n\r\nClient Remains Unresponsive\r\nFollow up four times, double-dial, and use the New Business Follow Up or New Business Follow Up Spanish label.\r\n\r\n\r\nCarrier Is Unresponsive\r\nAlert the team lead.\r\nHelpful Resources and Links\r\n* 📁 Tools, Scripts & Resources\r\n* EZLynx SalesCenter, Tarmika rater, Submission Center/Wunderrite, carrier websites, PURL links, CLUE/DHI reports, Calendly, Client Center, and approved underwriting research sources.\r\n* Department Coverage Standards and the Personal, Commercial, and Trucking line-of-business question libraries.\r\n* New Business Automations video, Hotshot Guidelines, approved CENT objection-handling framework, decline script, break-up process, Bad Contact memo, and follow-up labels.\r\n* Use the approved phone-script library for walk-in appointments, lead qualification, rapport, agency pitch, cross-selling, quote presentation, objections, follow-up, unreachable prospects, and win-back conversations.\r\n* Type NEW BUSINESS in the email template search to view all relevant email and text templates.\r\nTrucking Questions\r\n* Use the Trucking Line of Business question library.\r\nCommercial Questions\r\n* Use the Commercial Line of Business question library for the applicable coverage, including package, auto, bonds, liability, property, professional, cyber, workers compensation, and specialty lines.\r\nPersonal Questions\r\n* Use the Personal Line of Business question library for the applicable coverage, including auto, home, renters, condo, dwelling, flood, umbrella, recreational, watercraft, and specialty lines.\r\n* Source: https://sites.google.com/streetsmart.insurance/siteswiki/sops-standard-operating-procedures/new-business\r\nTraining Assets\r\nROBIE Reference Fields\r\nPurpose\r\nGuide the agency through receiving, qualifying, documenting, quoting, and assigning new-business opportunities.\r\nApplies To\r\nNew leads, quote requests, prospect intake, account qualification, carrier submissions, and new-business follow-up.\r\nSystems Used\r\nEZLynx, Submission Center, carrier portals, email, phone, Google Workspace, and approved quoting tools.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nRelated Items\r\n* BDR New Business Process SOP\r\n* Binding SOP\r\n* New Customer Policy Onboarding SOP\r\n* EZLynx application and policy-entry standards\r\n* Carrier-specific quoting skills and walkthrough videos\r\n* Document naming, upload, and file-maintenance standards"